  "description": {
    "text": "One of two premium file folders released on 18 March 2005 for the opening of the PokéPark theme park in Nagoya, each holding nine cards of Pokémon from the park's attractions and sold separately. The Blue file holds ordinary Pokémon cards, including Ho-Oh, Lugia, Kyogre, Groudon, Rayquaza and the three Legendary beasts, and all nine later came out in English in EX Emerald, EX Unseen Forces and POP Series 2. Together the nine illustrations form one mountain scene by Kouki Saitou, which also appears on the back of the folder, on a sticker inside and later on the English EX Collector's Window Tins.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: PokéPark Premium Files (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 8 September 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260908202020/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pok%C3%A9Park_Premium_Files_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A black wave-crest symbol at the bottom right, and a number out of 009",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: PokéPark Premium Files (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 8 September 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260908202020/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Pok%C3%A9Park_Premium_Files_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
